 videotape it on board and then  my son and an editor to put together the  final product over at Yahoo their CEO  Marissa Mayer made a few changes the  former Google executive band employees  working from home and led a campaign to  try and entice a younger audience in  create a list of favorite topic one of  the people to benefit from this was a 17  year old Nick dollar seal from London  yahoo paid a reported 18 million pounds  for his news app summly it uses an  algorithm to create bite-sized summaries  of news stories and even had backing  from Stephen Fry we caught up with Nick  back in March after rising for my  history exams I realized that Google and  being these search engines are quite  inefficient you have all of these  results but how do you decide what you  want to press on and so I thought that  summaries of previews would help you  decide so I coded it and it took about  two or three months and I got a  prototype out there in July of 2011 in  the investors context about a month  later 2013 was a great year for  television technology here's an o LED  screen brighter better black brighter  whites than ever before and that was  eclipsed in part by the rise and rise of  4k TV or ultra high-definition that's  four times better than your HD picture  and perhaps the biggest event of all  involved Twitter they went public in  November valued at a whopping 24 point  nine billion dollars despite having no  assets and no profit things didn't go  smoothly for facebook when they hand out  chairs the year before so the lack of  drama was almost a disappointment  well that's it for this year make sure  you keep up to date with all the tech  stories on the scan use for iPad app and  on our website sky news com we'll see  you in the new year
 

